  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `invoicing/currency.py`, and all 8 tests now pass, including `test_invoice_jpy`.\n\n**The bug:** `minor_units()` lowercased the currency code (`\"jpy\"`) and then looked it up in a list of uppercase codes (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). The lookup never matched, so yen and won were treated like currencies with cents. Yen totals were converted and printed with two decimal places, giving `\u00a514,118.50` instead of `\u00a514,118`.\n\n**The fix:** I changed `currency.lower()` to `currency.upper()` in that lookup. Now JPY and KRW correctly have no decimal places, both when the amount is converted and when"
